+++
title = "Filter Galleries"
template = "docs"
+++

Revela supports **virtual galleries** that automatically select images from a shared pool using filter expressions. Instead of manually organizing photos into folders, you define criteria and Revela builds the gallery dynamically.

<div class="features-grid">

### 📦 Single Source

Images stored once in `_images/` folder. No duplication needed.

### 🔄 Dynamic Updates

Galleries automatically update when images change or are added.

### 🔍 Powerful Queries

Filter by star rating, keywords, EXIF data, filename, date, and more with a simple syntax.

</div>

## Basic Setup

### 1. Create Shared Images Folder

Create an `_images/` folder (note the underscore prefix) in your source directory:

```
source/
├── _images/           # Shared images (not a gallery itself)
│   ├── photo-001.jpg
│   ├── photo-002.jpg
│   └── ...
├── canon/             # Filter gallery
│   └── _index.revela
├── sony/              # Filter gallery
│   └── _index.revela
└── _index.revela      # Homepage
```

### 2. Add Filter Expression

In each gallery's `_index.revela`, add a `filter` property:

```toml
+++
title = "Canon Photos"
filter = "exif.make == 'Canon'"
+++

All photos taken with Canon cameras.
```

---

## Filter Syntax

### Comparison Operators

| Operator | Description | Example |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `==` | Equal | `exif.make == 'Canon'` |
| `!=` | Not equal | `exif.make != 'Sony'` |
| `<` | Less than | `exif.iso < 800` |
| `<=` | Less than or equal | `exif.focalLength <= 35` |
| `>` | Greater than | `exif.iso > 1600` |
| `>=` | Greater than or equal | `exif.iso >= 3200` |

### Logical Operators

Combine conditions with `and`, `or`, and `not`:

```toml
# Both conditions must be true
filter = "exif.make == 'Canon' and exif.iso >= 800"

# Either condition can be true
filter = "exif.make == 'Canon' or exif.make == 'Sony'"

# Negate a condition
filter = "not exif.make == 'Canon'"
```

**Precedence:** `and` binds tighter than `or`. Use parentheses to change order:

```toml
# Evaluated as: a or (b and c)
filter = "exif.make == 'Canon' or exif.make == 'Sony' and exif.iso >= 800"

# Evaluated as: (a or b) and c
filter = "(exif.make == 'Canon' or exif.make == 'Sony') and exif.iso >= 800"
```

---

## Available Properties

### Image Properties

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `filename` | string | Image filename (e.g., `photo-001.jpg`) |
| `sourcePath` | string | Path within the source directory |
| `width` | int | Image width in pixels |
| `height` | int | Image height in pixels |
| `fileSize` | long | File size in bytes |
| `dateTaken` | DateTime | Date the photo was taken |
| `lastModified` | DateTime | File last-modified timestamp |

### Photo Metadata

Revela reads the XMP metadata that Capture One, Lightroom, and other photo
managers write into exported files:

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `rating` | int? | Star rating: `1`–`5`, `0` = unrated, `-1` = rejected; empty when the file has none |
| `keywords` | list | Keywords (e.g. `Selected`, `Startseite`) |
| `title` | string? | Photo title; falls back to the Windows title (EXIF `XPTitle`) |
| `description` | string? | Caption; falls back to the EXIF `ImageDescription` |

Test for a keyword with `contains(keywords, 'Startseite')`. It matches whole
keywords and ignores upper/lower case, so `Startseite-Archiv` does not match.

```toml
filter = "rating >= 4"
filter = "contains(keywords, 'Startseite')"
filter = "rating >= 4 and not contains(keywords, 'Privat')"
```

> **Export your metadata.** Revela can only read what is in the exported file.
> In Capture One, open the export recipe's **Metadata** tab and include the rating,
> keywords, and the title/description (IPTC) fields. In Lightroom Classic, set
> **Metadata** in the export dialog to *All Metadata* or *All Except Camera &
> Camera Raw Info*. Re-export the photos after changing the recipe.

### EXIF Properties

Access via `exif.` prefix:

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `exif.make` | string | Camera manufacturer |
| `exif.model` | string | Camera model |
| `exif.lensModel` | string | Lens name |
| `exif.fNumber` | double | Aperture (f/2.8 = 2.8) |
| `exif.exposureTime` | double | Shutter speed in seconds |
| `exif.iso` | int | ISO sensitivity |
| `exif.focalLength` | int | Focal length in mm |
| `exif.dateTaken` | DateTime | Capture date/time from EXIF |
| `exif.gpsLatitude` | double? | GPS latitude (if present) |
| `exif.gpsLongitude` | double? | GPS longitude (if present) |

### Raw EXIF Access

Access any EXIF tag via `exif.raw.TagName`:

```toml
filter = "exif.raw.Software == 'Lightroom'"
filter = "exif.raw.Artist == 'John Doe'"
```

Raw EXIF values are text, so compare them with text values.

---

## Built-in Functions

### Date Functions

| Function | Description | Example |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `year(date)` | Extract year | `year(dateTaken) == 2024` |
| `month(date)` | Extract month (1-12) | `month(dateTaken) == 12` |
| `day(date)` | Extract day (1-31) | `day(dateTaken) == 25` |

### String Functions

| Function | Description | Example |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `contains(str, substr)` | Check if contains | `contains(filename, 'portrait')` |
| `contains(keywords, word)` | Has this keyword (whole word, any case) | `contains(keywords, 'Startseite')` |
| `starts_with(str, prefix)` | Check prefix | `starts_with(filename, 'IMG_')` |
| `ends_with(str, suffix)` | Check suffix | `ends_with(filename, '-edit.jpg')` |
| `lower(str)` | To lowercase | `lower(exif.make) == 'canon'` |
| `upper(str)` | To uppercase | `upper(exif.make) == 'CANON'` |

---

## Pipe Syntax

Chain operations using the pipe `|` operator:

```
filter_expression | sort property [asc|desc] | limit n
filter_expression | sort random | limit n
```

### The `all` Keyword

Select all images without filtering:

```toml
filter = "all"
filter = "all | sort dateTaken desc"
filter = "all | sort dateTaken desc | limit 10"
```

### Sort Clause

Sort results by any property:

```toml
# Newest first
filter = "all | sort dateTaken desc"

# By EXIF property
filter = "exif.make == 'Canon' | sort exif.iso desc"
```

Photos without a value for the sort field (for example no ISO) come last, in both
directions; ties are broken by file name. Without a `| sort` clause, a filter gallery
uses the page's `sort` or the configured image sort, exactly like a folder gallery
(see [Sorting](../sorting/)).

### Random Order

`sort random` shuffles the matching photos. Combined with `limit`, it picks a
different selection each time:

```toml
# 15 random photos for the home page
filter = "all | sort random | limit 15"
```

The order is chosen while the pages are rendered, not when someone visits the site.
Every `revela generate pages` (and so every `revela generate all`) draws a new
selection, and the site stays the same between builds. A page `filter` and an
inline `[[gallery: …]]` block behave the same way, and within one build the grid,
the photo pages and their previous/next links all use the same order. To change it
regularly, run `revela generate all` on a schedule (for example a nightly task);
photos that are already processed are not processed again. `sort random` takes no
`asc`/`desc`.

### Limit Clause

Restrict the number of results:

```toml
# Only 5 images
filter = "all | limit 5"

# 10 newest photos
filter = "all | sort dateTaken desc | limit 10"
```

---

## Literal Values

### Strings

Single or double quotes both work:

```toml
filter = "filename == 'test.jpg'"
filter = "filename == \"test.jpg\""
```

### Numbers

```toml
filter = "exif.iso == 800"       # Integer
filter = "exif.fNumber == 2.8"   # Decimal
```

### Booleans & Null

```toml
filter = "exif.gpsLatitude != null"  # Has GPS data
filter = "exif.lensModel == null"    # No lens info
```

`true` and `false` are also valid literals.

---

## Common Patterns

### By Camera Brand

```toml
filter = "exif.make == 'Canon'"
filter = "exif.make == 'Sony'"
filter = "exif.make == 'Canon' or exif.make == 'Sony'"
```

### By Year

```toml
filter = "year(dateTaken) == 2024"
filter = "year(dateTaken) >= 2020 and year(dateTaken) <= 2024"
```

### High ISO (Low Light)

```toml
filter = "exif.iso >= 3200"
filter = "exif.iso >= 1600 | sort exif.iso desc"
```

### Wide Angle / Telephoto

```toml
filter = "exif.focalLength <= 35"   # Wide angle
filter = "exif.focalLength >= 85"   # Portrait/Telephoto
```

### Recent Photos (Homepage)

```toml
filter = "all | sort dateTaken desc | limit 5"
```

### Random Selection (Homepage)

```toml
filter = "all | sort random | limit 15"
```

### Best Rated

```toml
# All 4- and 5-star photos, best first
filter = "rating >= 4 | sort rating desc"

# 15 random photos from the best rated
filter = "rating >= 4 | sort random | limit 15"
```

`rating` comes from the XMP star rating that Capture One and Lightroom export
(see [Photo Metadata](#photo-metadata)). Photos without a
rating never match `rating >= 4` and are listed last by `sort rating`.

### By Keyword

```toml
filter = "contains(keywords, 'Startseite')"
filter = "contains(keywords, 'Startseite') | sort random | limit 15"
```

---

## Filter vs Sort

| Feature | Filter (`filter =`) | Sort (`sort =`) |
|---------|---------------------|-----------------|
| Purpose | Select images from `_images/` | Order images in any gallery |
| Scope | Creates virtual gallery | Works on existing images |
| Use case | Dynamic collections | Custom ordering |

You can use both together:

```toml
+++
filter = "exif.make == 'Canon'"
sort = "dateTaken:desc"
+++
```

---

## Error Handling

Invalid expressions fail the build with a position-aware message and a caret pointing at the problem:

```
Filter error: Expected expression, got ')'

  exif.make == ( )
              ^
```

Run `revela generate scan` to validate your filters before a full generation.

